**********************************************************************
*                                                                    *
*                                                                    *
*      FORCED BEGIN AND INITIALIZE ROUTINE                           *J
*                                                                    *
*                                                                    *
**********************************************************************

* FUNCTION   THE PURPOSE OF THIS ROUTINE IS TO INITIALIZE CERTAIN
*            PROGRAM CONSTANTS AND LVDA REGISTERS PRIOR TO EXECUTING
*            ANY PREFLIGHT ROUTINE. THIS ROUTINE SHALL BE ENTERED ONLY
*            FROM THE POWER UP ROUTINE, OR AS A RESULT OF AN RCA-110
*            INTERRUPT. THIS INTERRUPT IS USED WHEN THE LAUNCH COM-
*            PUTER TERMINATES AN LVDC ROUTINE PRIOR TO COMPLETION, OR
*            RE-INITIALIZES PROGRAM CONSTANTS AND CERTAIN LVDA REG-
*            ISTERS.

* ENTRIES    FBR1     ENTERED FROM POWER UP INITIALIZE
*            FBR2     ENTERED FROM RCA-110 INTERRUPT

       ORGSS   0,0,1,000,1,16,0

D.EMR  BSS     1
EMCON  BSS     1

FBR1   PIO     023          READ EMR AND SAVE                         B
       TRA     FBR3

FBR2   CLA     =O35770
       PIO     072          INHIBIT ALL INTERRUPTS EXCEPT TLC AND RCA I

       PIO     023
       AND     =O375377776  READ EMR, MASK EM8, EM3 AND 2 SPARE BITS  B
FBR3   STO     D.EMR        AND SAVE                                  B
*                           FIXME: LVDA MANUAL ONLY SHOWS ONE SPARE
       HOP     KIN400       HOP 400 INITIALIZE

       CLA     =O000001002
       PIO     022          SET ICR'S 1 + 9, RESET ALL ICR'S EXCEPT   B
       XOR     D.KONS       1 AND 9                                   B
       PIO     026

       CLA     =O265252260
       HOP     ISS          ISSUE STATUS CODE                         P
       TRA     *
